n><span class="enc-snip">The Göktürk–Sasanian destruction of the Hephthalites was a joint campaign around 557 CE that ended the Hephthalite empire in Central Asia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gol-gumbaz"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gol-gumbaz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gol Gumbaz</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gol Gumbaz is the mausoleum of Sultan Muhammad Adil Shah of the Bijapur Sultanate at Bijapur in Karnataka, India, completed around 1656.</span></a></li></ul>
